WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.062 --> 00:00:09.096
&gt;&gt; Welcome back, the U.S. And

00:00:10.064 --> 00:00:10.431
western officials are seeing

00:00:10.698 --> 00:00:11.165
signs that Ukraine's

00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:12.566
counteroffensive is already

00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:13.000
underway.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:14.234
Military intelligence officials

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:15.302
tell CNN that the Ukrainian

00:00:15.569 --> 00:00:17.137
forces have begun testing

00:00:18.072 --> 00:00:18.305
Russian positions.

00:00:18.972 --> 00:00:20.207
The artillery strikes and

00:00:20.474 --> 00:00:22.076
ground attacks, searching for

00:00:22.309 --> 00:00:22.576
vulnerabilities.

00:00:22.843 --> 00:00:24.211
This long awaited

00:00:24.478 --> 00:00:25.079
counteroffensive is expected to

00:00:25.345 --> 00:00:26.280
be carried out on multiple

00:00:26.547 --> 00:00:26.680
fronts.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.315
This is nearly 16 months after

00:00:28.582 --> 00:00:29.316
Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.085
Joining us this morning is mark

00:00:31.351 --> 00:00:32.953
Esper, who served as defense

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:33.654
secretary under president

00:00:34.088 --> 00:00:34.288
trump.

00:00:34.288 --> 00:00:34.822
Secretary expert, good morning,

00:00:35.089 --> 00:00:35.723
and thank you.

00:00:38.392 --> 00:00:39.593
&gt;&gt; Good morning.

00:00:40.094 --> 00:00:40.527
&gt;&gt; What needs to happen for

00:00:40.794 --> 00:00:41.762
this counteroffensive to be

00:00:42.096 --> 00:00:42.629
successful?

00:00:42.896 --> 00:00:43.397
&gt;&gt; I think that what needs to

00:00:43.664 --> 00:00:44.298
happen to us what seemed to be

00:00:44.565 --> 00:00:44.832
underway right.

00:00:45.099 --> 00:00:46.366
Now they're conducting shaping

00:00:46.633 --> 00:00:47.601
operations for the last couple

00:00:48.102 --> 00:00:50.337
weeks or so, bombing refineries,

00:00:50.604 --> 00:00:51.405
knocking out rail lines, et

00:00:51.672 --> 00:00:52.106
cetera.

00:00:52.106 --> 00:00:52.673
But now we are in the part of

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.475
the phase that we call

00:00:54.742 --> 00:00:56.543
recognizance where small

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.312
armored units go out and probe

00:00:58.579 --> 00:00:59.480
the 600-mile front line if you

00:00:59.747 --> 00:01:01.248
will to try and find the

00:01:01.515 --> 00:01:02.416
weaknesses, and the strong

00:01:02.683 --> 00:01:02.816
points.

00:01:03.083 --> 00:01:03.617
And I think that once they

00:01:04.118 --> 00:01:05.419
figure that out, you will start

00:01:05.686 --> 00:01:06.553
seeing that the main effort

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.356
emerges very quickly along with

00:01:09.623 --> 00:01:10.324
supporting efforts to really

00:01:10.591 --> 00:01:11.391
push the Russians back in both

00:01:11.658 --> 00:01:12.126
the east and the south.

00:01:12.326 --> 00:01:13.494
And it will be quite dramatic,

00:01:14.294 --> 00:01:14.461
I expect.

00:01:14.728 --> 00:01:16.530
&gt;&gt; Secretary, one of the things

00:01:16.797 --> 00:01:17.431
I picked up over the course of

00:01:17.698 --> 00:01:18.465
the last several months both

00:01:18.732 --> 00:01:20.367
here in the U.S. But also

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:21.335
talking and European

00:01:21.602 --> 00:01:22.469
counterparts as well, is that I

00:01:22.736 --> 00:01:24.404
think it was captured by David

00:01:24.671 --> 00:01:25.572
ignatius in the Washington

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:26.406
post.

00:01:26.406 --> 00:01:27.574
It said that if Ukraine can

00:01:28.142 --> 00:01:29.343
drive back an already shaky

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:30.544
Russian army, it stands a

00:01:30.811 --> 00:01:32.579
chance in Moscow to bargain for

00:01:32.846 --> 00:01:33.680
an end to the failed invasion.

00:01:34.148 --> 00:01:35.315
But if Ukraine fails, would be

00:01:35.582 --> 00:01:37.284
a bitter blow to the country's

00:01:37.551 --> 00:01:38.452
population and could endanger

00:01:39.353 --> 00:01:40.287
continue support from some

00:01:40.554 --> 00:01:41.488
restless nato members.

00:01:42.289 --> 00:01:43.524
I think the question I have had

00:01:43.791 --> 00:01:45.526
leading up to this moment is

00:01:45.793 --> 00:01:48.395
how, is this a do or die moment

00:01:48.662 --> 00:01:50.397
to use a poor cliché for the

00:01:50.664 --> 00:01:52.633
Ukrainian forces for Ukraine in

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:53.300
this conflict right now?

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:57.171
&gt;&gt; It's a very significant

00:01:57.437 --> 00:01:57.571
moment.

00:01:57.838 --> 00:01:58.539
Everybody is looking to Ukraine

00:01:58.806 --> 00:01:59.506
to be very successful.

00:02:00.174 --> 00:02:01.341
You know, I was in Europe two

00:02:01.608 --> 00:02:02.643
weeks ago for about two weeks,

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:03.577
and the number one question

00:02:03.844 --> 00:02:05.245
over there is, where is U.S.

00:02:05.512 --> 00:02:05.646
Support?

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.247
And everybody fairly things

00:02:08.282 --> 00:02:10.450
that if Ukraine does, well U.S.

00:02:10.717 --> 00:02:11.084
Import will continue.

00:02:11.385 --> 00:02:12.553
If, not it could weather, and

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.321
if your support weathers, then

00:02:14.588 --> 00:02:15.556
a lot of other countries will

00:02:15.823 --> 00:02:16.190
go with it.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.457
So it is very important and I

00:02:17.724 --> 00:02:18.425
think Ukraine understands as

00:02:18.692 --> 00:02:19.426
politically, not just

00:02:19.693 --> 00:02:21.461
militarily, but they have a

00:02:22.196 --> 00:02:22.462
very successful

00:02:22.729 --> 00:02:23.030
counteroffensive.

00:02:23.297 --> 00:02:23.764
It shows people a return on

00:02:24.198 --> 00:02:24.431
their investment in the

00:02:24.698 --> 00:02:25.032
Ukrainian military.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.202
&gt;&gt; We know that some groups of

00:02:28.435 --> 00:02:29.203
Ukrainian pilots have just are

00:02:29.469 --> 00:02:30.204
traveling to the uk to get

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:31.305
trained on these f-16 fighter

00:02:31.572 --> 00:02:31.672
jets.

00:02:32.206 --> 00:02:33.440
There were lawmakers in the

00:02:33.707 --> 00:02:36.210
U.S. Who said that we should be

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:37.244
trained as pilots before we

00:02:37.511 --> 00:02:38.378
even made the decision to allow

00:02:38.645 --> 00:02:40.214
the f-16s to go, because it

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:41.315
takes months, at least four, to

00:02:41.582 --> 00:02:42.316
get them trained up.

00:02:42.583 --> 00:02:44.218
Are they necessary in this

00:02:44.284 --> 00:02:45.152
counteroffensive at the front

00:02:45.419 --> 00:02:45.485
end?

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:47.221
&gt;&gt; I think it would be very

00:02:47.487 --> 00:02:49.056
important to have them on board

00:02:49.323 --> 00:02:50.224
now, but clearly, it won't

00:02:50.457 --> 00:02:50.591
happen.

00:02:50.958 --> 00:02:52.392
Clearly, we are conducting a

00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:54.228
combined arms offense, which

00:02:54.461 --> 00:02:56.230
means that heavy armored forces,

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.232
mechanized infantry, artillery,

00:02:58.365 --> 00:03:00.234
et cetera, it would be helpful

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:00.901
to have a long range strike

00:03:01.168 --> 00:03:05.072
aircraft that could hit targets,

00:03:05.339 --> 00:03:06.240
tactical or support from those

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:07.241
units as well, and how clear

00:03:07.507 --> 00:03:08.342
the skies of Russian aircraft.

00:03:08.976 --> 00:03:11.011
At that won't be available.

00:03:11.278 --> 00:03:12.412
I think the administration is

00:03:12.679 --> 00:03:14.948
to blame for being late in

00:03:15.215 --> 00:03:16.250
terms of delivering the most

00:03:16.383 --> 00:03:17.150
vital items, whether it's

00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:18.252
Abrams tanks or f-16 aircraft.

00:03:20.888 --> 00:03:22.923
&gt;&gt; Mister secretary, to pulley

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.258
paraphrase one of your price,

00:03:24.625 --> 00:03:25.893
answers you put war with the

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:26.860
army that you have, and the

00:03:27.127 --> 00:03:27.461
army that you want.

00:03:27.761 --> 00:03:29.029
There's been some divergence I

00:03:29.296 --> 00:03:30.264
think what U.S. Officials have

00:03:30.364 --> 00:03:31.231
been saying publicly about the

00:03:31.498 --> 00:03:32.833
readiness of Ukraine, of its

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.768
forces in this moment, versus

00:03:35.035 --> 00:03:35.903
maybe what the reality is

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.838
behind the effort to surge

00:03:38.272 --> 00:03:38.538
equipment.

00:03:38.538 --> 00:03:39.806
Do you think that Ukrainian

00:03:40.274 --> 00:03:40.507
forces are ready to have a

00:03:40.774 --> 00:03:41.241
successful counteroffensive?

00:03:41.508 --> 00:03:44.645
&gt;&gt; But what I can read and

00:03:44.912 --> 00:03:45.646
between the lines, I've talked

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.180
a lot of folks in Europe

00:03:47.447 --> 00:03:49.283
recently, they have enough, but

00:03:49.549 --> 00:03:50.284
they can do better if they have

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:51.485
far more, particularly of

00:03:51.752 --> 00:03:53.420
course again, at 60 aircraft to

00:03:53.687 --> 00:03:54.354
support them.

00:03:54.621 --> 00:03:55.689
It is unclear whether they have

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:57.658
the numbers of states they

00:03:57.925 --> 00:03:58.292
need.

00:03:58.292 --> 00:03:59.559
But, look at this, point they

00:04:00.294 --> 00:04:00.661
have to move forward on the

00:04:00.928 --> 00:04:01.495
counter offensive.

00:04:01.762 --> 00:04:02.396
We need to push the Russians

00:04:02.663 --> 00:04:04.298
back, they need to show success,

00:04:04.431 --> 00:04:05.365
because it will not just help

00:04:05.632 --> 00:04:06.300
them on the battlefield, but

00:04:06.566 --> 00:04:07.367
it's going to have them again

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:08.302
with western allies and

00:04:08.302 --> 00:04:08.702
continue allied support.

00:04:08.969 --> 00:04:11.405
&gt;&gt; John Bolton has an

00:04:11.672 --> 00:04:12.606
interesting opinion piece in

00:04:12.873 --> 00:04:13.540
the Wall Street journal today

00:04:13.807 --> 00:04:14.541
where he takes on the Biden

00:04:15.309 --> 00:04:16.343
administration, particularly on

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:16.710
Iran.

00:04:16.977 --> 00:04:17.477
That's not surprising.

00:04:18.312 --> 00:04:20.347
What is interesting I think is

00:04:20.614 --> 00:04:21.548
how he ties together what we

00:04:21.815 --> 00:04:24.351
are seeing in terms of

00:04:24.618 --> 00:04:24.985
alliances and changing

00:04:25.252 --> 00:04:26.420
alliances, and a close

00:04:26.687 --> 00:04:27.187
relationship that we're seeing

00:04:27.454 --> 00:04:28.388
between China and Russia.

00:04:28.655 --> 00:04:29.623
How the uae and Saudi Arabia

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:32.359
play into it, given the

00:04:32.626 --> 00:04:33.527
increasing concerns about Iran.

00:04:34.328 --> 00:04:35.395
Here's what he writes.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.297
The uae and others are now more

00:04:37.564 --> 00:04:38.332
open to Russia and China.

00:04:38.565 --> 00:04:40.334
These tectonic developments are

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:40.534
--

00:04:41.301 --> 00:04:42.336
pending strategic failure from

00:04:42.602 --> 00:04:43.403
America and its key allies.

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:44.338
Do you agree?

00:04:45.272 --> 00:04:46.340
&gt;&gt; Well, look.

00:04:46.573 --> 00:04:48.342
We need to shift towards the

00:04:48.575 --> 00:04:49.276
focus on China as a greater

00:04:49.543 --> 00:04:51.345
tragic threat that we face in a

00:04:51.611 --> 00:04:51.745
century.

00:04:52.012 --> 00:04:52.512
But if you do so in a way that

00:04:52.779 --> 00:04:55.315
does not create a vacuum and

00:04:55.582 --> 00:04:56.350
clearly, tournaments and the

00:04:56.516 --> 00:04:56.717
Middle East.

00:04:56.984 --> 00:04:58.352
Time is a net energy importer,

00:04:58.618 --> 00:04:59.453
which is why they want access

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:01.288
to both the Middle East and to

00:05:01.555 --> 00:05:02.356
Russia by the way, and so we

00:05:02.622 --> 00:05:03.590
want to maintain a presence.

00:05:03.857 --> 00:05:04.491
I think the administration is

00:05:04.758 --> 00:05:06.360
working its relationship with

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:07.294
Saudi Arabia and others in the

00:05:07.561 --> 00:05:07.694
region.

00:05:08.362 --> 00:05:09.396
But look, we also see Iran

00:05:09.663 --> 00:05:10.364
emerging.

00:05:10.464 --> 00:05:12.366
It's not like a top weapons

00:05:12.532 --> 00:05:13.333
supplier to Russia, as is

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:13.700
China.

00:05:13.967 --> 00:05:15.569
So you see these boxcar shaping

00:05:15.836 --> 00:05:16.503
up out there in the global

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:17.537
environment, and so it's

00:05:17.804 --> 00:05:19.473
important we stay there.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:20.374
&gt;&gt; Started 70 secretary, but

00:05:20.607 --> 00:05:21.208
what do you mean the

00:05:21.475 --> 00:05:22.376
administration is to workouts

00:05:22.609 --> 00:05:23.443
relationship with Saudi Arabia?

00:05:24.378 --> 00:05:26.380
President Biden went there to

00:05:26.646 --> 00:05:29.216
the consternation of many, how

00:05:29.483 --> 00:05:33.253
this bond, and then OPEC just

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:33.854
slashed productions.

00:05:34.388 --> 00:05:35.522
&gt;&gt; Tony blinken's there right

00:05:35.789 --> 00:05:35.856
now.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.457
&gt;&gt; Tony blinken's having these

00:05:37.724 --> 00:05:38.425
meetings with a very cordial

00:05:38.692 --> 00:05:39.226
statement they came out

00:05:39.493 --> 00:05:39.659
yesterday.

00:05:39.926 --> 00:05:40.594
What does improvement look like

00:05:40.861 --> 00:05:41.561
to you, or work on to you.

00:05:42.396 --> 00:05:44.398
&gt;&gt; I think work on is Tony

00:05:44.598 --> 00:05:44.865
blinken's visit.

00:05:45.232 --> 00:05:46.466
I think that is important.

00:05:46.733 --> 00:05:47.534
But clearly, the relationship

00:05:47.801 --> 00:05:49.269
is not where it needs to be

00:05:49.536 --> 00:05:49.736
between us.

00:05:50.404 --> 00:05:52.406
We saw a few months ago, China

00:05:52.539 --> 00:05:53.440
brokered that peace treaty, if

00:05:53.707 --> 00:05:55.342
you will, between the Saudis

00:05:55.609 --> 00:05:56.543
and Iran, and that was not a

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:57.411
good development.

00:05:57.677 --> 00:06:00.414
And so I think it just requires

00:06:00.514 --> 00:06:00.614
work.

00:06:00.881 --> 00:06:01.548
Not just with the Saudis, that

00:06:01.815 --> 00:06:04.484
the uae, Kuwait, Bahrain, and

00:06:04.751 --> 00:06:05.452
others in the region, to which

00:06:05.719 --> 00:06:06.053
we have a long term

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:06.553
relationship.

